  "body": "<!--\r\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nThis change removes the explicit non-propagation of the referrer for dynamic `import()` calls, and fixes https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3744. By doing so, it aligns fetching static and dynamic imports.\r\n\r\nNote that the spec doesn't include the explicit exception for `import()` because it has been explicitly wanted, but because this distinction happened accidentally when static and dynamic imports had two separate paths and I had to add it explicitly when unifying them in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8253.\r\n\r\nFirefox currently implements the new behavior, while Webkit and Chroimum implement the old behavior.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   * Chroimum (https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9407#issuecomment-1603128150)\r\n   * Geko (https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9407#issuecomment-1613442828)\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/40474\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1461987\r\n   * Gecko: already implemented\r\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=258848\r\n   * ~~Deno~~ Deno only passes the `Accept`, `Accept-Encoding`, `Host` and `User-Agent` headers\r\n   * ~~Node.js~~ Node.js only passes the `Accept`, `Connection` and `Host` headers\r\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: n/a\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9407/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 29, 2023, 4:16 PM UTC (3b3681f)\">/webappapis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9407/8f3d1fc...3b3681f/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 29, 2023, 4:16 PM UTC (3b3681f)\">diff</a> )",
